# Bottom Navigation Layout Rules

Locked files: `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`, rendered once as a **direct child of `<body>`** in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Do not add a second nav in pages. Do not wrap it in `<main>`, flex shells, or page layouts.

- Do NOT `position: fixed` on `html`/`body`. That makes the nav a descendant of an already-inset box and lifts it in the Home Screen PWA (Safari still looks fine).
- The outer `<nav>` stays `fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 w-full bg-background border-t border-border/30 transform-none`. Height is CSS-only: 50px in Safari, `calc(50px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))` in standalone.
- Inner icon row MUST remain `flex h-[50px] w-full shrink-0 items-center justify-around px-2` (never `h-full` once the standalone bar is taller).
- Do NOT add `pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]` on the icon row. In standalone, only the **nav height** grows: `calc(50px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))` so the background fills the home indicator and icons stay in the top 50px.
- Do NOT `transform` or hide the nav on scroll or route change.

`main.app-scroll` is **always** `overflow: hidden` with `pb-[60px]` (standalone adds `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` to that clearance).
Every route uses `PageShell`. Do not add a second `pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]` on pages.
`PageHeader` is not sticky.
